## Base URL for the Django API. Leave unset in local dev — the Vite dev
## server proxies /api and /media to http://localhost:8000 (see vite.config.ts),
## so requests can go to the relative path below with no CORS involved.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api/v1

## In production (Vercel) the frontend and the Django API are on two
## different domains (a Vercel static deployment has no backend of its own
## to proxy to), so the relative default above would just 404 against
## Vercel itself. Set this to the deployed backend's absolute URL instead —
## in the Vercel project's Settings → Environment Variables, NOT in this
## file — e.g.:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://<your-backend>.up.railway.app/api/v1
